The database schema for the meeting invite system is complete. Let me provide a summary of what was accomplished in this iteration:

## Summary

I've completed the database schema and functions for Phase 4: Invite System. Here's what was created:

### New Tables
1. **`roiheimen.meeting_invite`** - Invite codes for joining meetings
   - `id`, `meeting_id`, `code` (unique 8-char alphanumeric), `max_uses`, `uses_count`, `expires_at`, `created_by`, `created_at`

2. **`roiheimen.meeting_participant`** - Users who have joined meetings
   - `id`, `meeting_id`, `user_id`, `display_name`, `participant_num`, `is_organizer`, `joined_via`, `created_at`
   - Unique constraints on (meeting_id, user_id) and (meeting_id, participant_num)

### New Functions
- `create_invite_code(meeting_id, max_uses, expires_at)` - Creates invite codes (8-char, no confusing chars)
- `validate_invite_code(code)` - Validates and returns meeting info
- `join_meeting(meeting_id, invite_code, display_name)` - Joins user as participant
- `get_meeting_token(meeting_id)` - Returns meeting-scoped JWT for queue.html access
- `delete_invite_code(invite_id)` - Deletes an invite
- `get_meeting_invites(meeting_id)` - Lists all invites for a meeting
- `get_meeting_participants(meeting_id)` - Lists all participants

### RLS Policies
- Org admins/owners can manage invites
- Participants and org members can view participants  
- Users can add themselves via join_meeting function

### Files Modified/Created
- `pkg/server/db.sql` - Main schema file
- `pkg/server/migrations/018-meeting-invites.sql` - Migration file

### Next Steps (for future iterations)
- Create UI components: `/bli-med.html`, `/i/{code}` pages
- Create components: `invite-generator.js`, `invite-list.js`, `join-meeting.js`, `qr-code.js`
- Update `manage.html` with "Invitasjonar" tab
- Write E2E tests for the invite system
